=== p2-windows · W7 · page:settings/Privacy (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:settings/Privacy   kind=page   web route=/account/privacy
Web source  : web/src/features/settings/pages/PrivacyPage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/PrivacyPage/** (+ shell registration, tests)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300), maui-windows workload installed — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repo's WinUI app is code-first C# (no per-page .xaml). Every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (Microsoft.UI-free Registration / value
  types / diagnostics — unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (state holder), <Name>.Source.cs (data
  sources) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's idealized "PrivacyPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs
  under TeslaSync/Features/Settings" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface registers with the W4
  ShellPageFactory by route name ("Privacy"), which RouteTable already maps to account/privacy
  (RouteTable.cs:152 Page("Privacy","account/privacy",SettingsAccountIntegrations,"Privacy")) and which the
  footer "Account" shortcut (ShellWindow.xaml.cs CreateFooterItem("account/privacy","Account")) already targets
  — until now that route resolved to RoutePendingView; it now resolves to the real PrivacyPage.
- The web page is a thin PageContainer hosting <PrivacySection/> (PrivacyPage.tsx wraps PrivacySection 1:1; all
  browser-local state — recent-pages LRU, cookie/consent machinery, confirmation dialog, toast feedback — lives
  inside that component). Ported 1:1 as a thin PrivacyPage (shared PageContainer: title + subtitle + copy-link)
  hosting the already-ported native PrivacySection (W3), which reproduces the web component's shield-headed
  header and EVERY region: the recent-pages clearer (stored-entries counter + destructive TsConfirmDialog-gated
  "Clear recent pages" with the "Don't ask again" silence opt-in) and the cookie / analytics consent manager
  (current-decision label, consent-aware body copy, grant / withdraw / reset actions), plus the requirement
  read's loading / live / stale / offline / error freshness chip + retry — never hiding a panel. Mirrors the
  sibling TwoFactorAuthPage (thin page over TotpEnrollmentSection).
- Manifest models this unit as "no API data sources — renders from navigation params / local state"
  (requiredCount=2, the two page-tier strings; no panels/charts/maps/data-states declared at the page tier). The
  only backend-touching read is the hosted section's deployment-wide require_cookie_consent flag (web
  useVersionInfo). The shell-registered (parameterless) page hosts the section against a no-backend
  EmptyConsentRequirementSource (PrivacyPage.Source.cs) that emits the cache-then-network sequence
  Loading -> Empty; the section view-model coalesces Empty to "consent not required" + the preview body copy —
  exactly the web Boolean(versionQuery.data?.require_cookie_consent) reading of undefined as false — so the page
  is fully mountable with no backend, mirroring the EmptyActiveSessionsFeed / open-mode-controller convention the
  sibling W7 account pages use. A host behind a configured backend injects the repository-backed
  ConsentRequirementSource through the DI constructor. The recent-pages clearer and the consent grant/withdraw/
  reset controls are pure client-side surfaces and stay fully live regardless. No non-SI fields exist on this
  privacy surface, so the P1/S5 converters are N/A here.
- Strings: the two page-tier keys are absent from the platform catalog (apps/windows/Strings/{en,ar,he}/
  Resources.resw is AUTO-GENERATED by apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts — "do not edit by hand"); the web
  resolves account.privacy.title/subtitle as inline t(key, default) fallbacks. The native surface resolves them
  the same way — keyed ILocalizer.GetString(key, <same English default>) flowing through ShellLocalizer ->
  shell Localization (resw lookup -> English fallback) — so the auto-generated catalog is left untouched, exactly
  as the sibling ActiveSessionsPage (account.sessions.title/subtitle) does. Zero hardcoded literals; every label
  flows through the i18n facade with the web key names. The three Microsoft.UI-free sources (Model / Source /
  ViewModel) are Compile-linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests for headless coverage.

=== PARITY ===
PARITY_REQUIRED=2

# Strings (2) — every visible literal resolves through the ILocalizer facade (resw lookup -> English fallback)
# with the web key names; no hardcoded literals in the view.
[x] string - account.privacy.subtitle -> PrivacyPageRegistration.Subtitle (PrivacyPage.Model.cs)
      localizer.GetString("account.privacy.subtitle",
        "Manage browser-local data: recently viewed pages and cookies / analytics consent.");
      rendered PrivacyPage.cs PageContainer.Subtitle (PageContainer ctor)
[x] string - account.privacy.title    -> PrivacyPageRegistration.Title (PrivacyPage.Model.cs)
      localizer.GetString("account.privacy.title", "Privacy");
      rendered PrivacyPage.cs PageContainer title (PageContainer ctor) + AutomationProperties.Name

PARITY_COVERED=2
# Coverage asserted headlessly (TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/PrivacyPageTests.cs):
#   ViewModel_resolves_every_required_string_key records both keys through a RecordingLocalizer;
#   Registration_resolves_the_two_page_strings_with_web_defaults asserts the web English defaults;
#   Registration_uses_the_web_key_names_for_the_two_page_strings pins the key names verbatim;
#   Registration_mirrors_the_web_route_and_nav_name pins route/slug;
#   Registration_builds_the_copy_link_deep_link_for_the_route pins the account/privacy copy-link;
#   EmptyConsentRequirementSource_streams_loading_then_a_successful_empty and _honors_a_cancelled_token pin the
#   no-backend default's contract.

# Beyond the 2 required page-tier strings, the hosted PrivacySection reproduces every region of the web source
# (web/src/features/settings/components/PrivacySection.tsx), each verified headlessly by PrivacySectionTests:
#   Panel    — one glass panel (web GlassPanel) with the shield-icon header (privacy.title / privacy.subtitle).
#   Recent   — recently-viewed-pages clearer: stored-entries counter (recentPages.storedCount), Clear button
#              disabled at 0 (recentPages.clearButton), destructive ConfirmDialog (recentPages.clearConfirm*)
#              with the silenceKey "Don't ask again" opt-in, success status line (recentPages.cleared).
#   Consent  — cookie / analytics consent manager: current-decision label (consent.state.*), require-consent
#              -aware body copy (consent.section.bodyOn / bodyOff), grant / withdraw / reset actions
#              (consent.action.*) each disabled on the matching state, success status lines (consent.toast.*).
#   States   — the require_cookie_consent read's loading / ready(live) / stale / offline / error freshness, each
#              a visible chip + retry that never hides the panel (web Boolean(undefined) === false fallback).

